{
  "name": "Hikyaku - Escalate failed deliveries to dispatch",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3f59bb24-d256-4866-b3fa-b54f16be8d05",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [220, 40],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## Setup\n1. Open **Hikyaku Delivery Status Trigger** and connect your **Hikyaku OAuth2 API** credential.\n2. In **Statuses**, pick whatever your exception states are (e.g. **failed_delivery**, **returned**) — they load live from your instance.\n3. The **IF** node branches on `warehouse_id` being set as a placeholder — replace this with your own escalation rule (time of day, specific warehouse, etc.).\n4. Open **Alert Dispatch Team** and connect an SMTP credential.\n5. Activate the workflow."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "151ae720-a484-436f-8434-cf78b818a128",
      "name": "Hikyaku Delivery Status Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-hikyaku.hikyakuDeliveryStatusTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [240, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "statuses": []
      },
      "notes": "Set Statuses to your exception states, e.g. failed_delivery, returned.",
      "credentials": {
        "hikyakuOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL",
          "name": "Hikyaku OAuth2 API account"
        }
      }
    },
